{%- comment -%}
  Product register — the two-register firewall, in one place.

  Outputs exactly one word: `original` or `inspired`.
  Callers capture it:

    {%- capture register -%}
      {%- render 'product-register', product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign register = register | strip -%}
    {%- if register == 'original' -%} ... {%- endif -%}

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  The rule is currently derived from `product.vendor`, and the vendor
  posture is an OPEN DECISION (reference-analysis/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md
  §7.4). When it is settled — most likely by migrating to an
  `inspired_by` metafield — this file is the only one that changes.
  Nothing else in the theme may test vendor directly.

  ⚠ WHAT `vendor` ACTUALLY HOLDS
  On this store `product.vendor` is NOT a brand. It holds the name of
  the designer fragrance a product is inspired by — 42 distinct values
  across 56 products, e.g. "Bleu De Chanel Parfum".
  `04-PRODUCTS.md` §1: "A rebuild must never render `product.vendor` as
  a brand." Only 16 of 56 carry a Siwa-authored vendor.

  THE SPLIT
    original -> 16 products. Vendor is `Siwa Fragrances` or
                `Siwa original creation`. May carry heritage language,
                Arabic naming, Siwan motifs and the Cultural Accent Set.
    inspired -> 40 products. Commercial framing and UI Chrome only.
                Cultural Accent here is a firewall breach.

  Source: Planning/BENCHMARK.md Part 2 §5, reference-analysis/04-PRODUCTS.md §1.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign vendor_handle = product.vendor | handle
  if vendor_handle == 'siwa-fragrances' or vendor_handle == 'siwa-original-creation'
    echo 'original'
  else
    echo 'inspired'
  endif
-%}
